WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.537
Post-quantum cryptography prepares systems for a future where certain current public-key algorithms may no longer provide adequate protection.

2
00:00:09.537 --> 00:00:16.327
It does not require defenders to run quantum computers, and it is not the same as quantum key distribution.

3
00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:29.679
It is a standards-aware migration effort for ordinary systems that depend on key establishment, digital signatures, certificates, software signing, remote access, identity, and trusted communication.

4
00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:34.333
The most important planning move is to understand cryptographic roles.

5
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:38.453
A key encapsulation mechanism helps establish shared secrets.

6
00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:42.421
A digital signature supports authentication and integrity.

7
00:00:42.421 --> 00:00:48.448
Symmetric encryption and hashing have different risk profiles than public-key mechanisms.

8
00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:59.740
Once roles are clear, teams can build an inventory that records where cryptography is used, what depends on it, what data it protects, who owns it, and how migration-ready it is.

9
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:10.803
A strong migration program prioritizes risk, uses vetted standards and mature libraries, tests interoperability, coordinates with vendors, and builds crypto agility.

10
00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:16.983
It avoids custom cryptography and avoids unsupported combinations that cannot be maintained.

11
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:29.343
It also recognizes that engineering details matter: size, performance, certificates, protocols, hardware, logging, monitoring, and operational support can all shape the migration path.

12
00:01:29.343 --> 00:01:33.157
The goal is not to predict the exact date of a quantum threat.

13
00:01:33.157 --> 00:01:38.956
The goal is to reduce future migration risk before urgent replacement becomes necessary.

14
00:01:38.956 --> 00:01:48.188
Teams that start with inventory, governance, pilots, and practical communication will be better prepared than teams that wait for a deadline.

15
00:01:48.188 --> 00:01:57.649
PQC is ultimately a resilience project: know what you depend on, make change possible, and move deliberately toward standards-based protection.
